module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.empty_capture_read_as_clean_result

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data empty_capture_read_as_clean_result: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "empty_capture_read_as_clean_result" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an empty capture read as a clean result** (an instrument refuses on one stream while the reader keeps the other, so the capture is EMPTY and the empty capture is consumed as a finding of nothing. ",

    "It is a specialization of [[absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked]] -- cited here until 2026-09-07 by the nickname `blank is not evidence`, which is the DESIGN section 3 defect this ledger polices and, measured, a DELETED EDGE: the family audit identity join over the nine members could not see this citation at all, so the one boundary the family had read as zero -- narrowed to a mechanism that recurs: the refusal is well-formed and honest, it simply travels on a channel nobody kept. ",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, reading a failing CI job during gunbc PR 9984: `gh run view --job <id> --log > f` writes ZERO BYTES and puts `run is still in progress; logs will be available when it is complete` on stderr, so the redirect captures nothing while the job is already recorded as completed failure. ",

    "A grep for `panicked` or `FAILED` over that file then reports no failures for a job that failed. ",

    "Two adjacent instances in the same call: `gh api .../actions/jobs/<id>/logs` writes zero bytes without --allow-escape-sequences, again refusing on stderr; and the same subcommand takes a JOB id rather than a run id, where the wrong id also yields nothing useful. ",

    "THE ASYMMETRY IS WHAT MAKES IT RECUR: the failure direction is always benign. ",

    "An empty capture never manufactures a false alarm, only a false all-clear, so nothing in the reader's experience trains them to check it. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable at the reading site -- measuring the capture's size before consuming it converts the silent case into a loud one -- and silent wrongness wherever that check is absent, which is the default. ",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable for instruments this repository owns, since a reader that must consume a typed outcome cannot consume a byte count of zero as a verdict; it stays mitigatable for third-party command-line tools, whose stream discipline is outside the modeled guarantee and is observed rather than proven. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a repository instrument-reading surface whose result type distinguishes READ SUCCESSFULLY AND FOUND NOTHING from DID NOT READ, sufficient that a zero-byte capture cannot inhabit the first -- at which point the diligence rule below is subsumed for every call routed through it, and remains diligence for calls that are not. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: before believing a quiet result, ask which stream the instrument refuses on and which stream you kept. ",

    "If a refusal and a clean result produce the same bytes in the channel you read, you have no observation. ",

    "The mechanical form, and it is a two-step rather than a byte-count rule, because inferring failure from size alone fabricates a refusal for the query that legitimately returned nothing: a zero-byte capture is NOT A VERDICT IN EITHER DIRECTION, so consult the instrument's typed status -- its exit code, and the stream its refusal travels on -- before consuming the emptiness. ",

    "Where the status says the instrument ran and the capture is empty, that is FOUND NOTHING and is a real observation; where the status says it refused, or the status is unavailable, the capture is DID NOT READ and no conclusion may be drawn from it. ",

    "The failure of the original habit is not that it read zero as one of those two, it is that it read zero WITHOUT ASKING which. ",

    "FOURTH INSTANCE, 2026-09-02, gunbc PR 10078, AND IT DEFEATS BOTH RULES ABOVE AS WRITTEN: reading the newly promoted aggregate's receipt line via `gh api .../actions/jobs/<id>/logs` produced NINETY-NINE BYTES ON STDOUT -- the refusal string `the response contains terminal escape sequences; pass --allow-escape-sequences to output it anyway` written into the PAYLOAD channel rather than onto stderr. ",

    "Both steps of the mechanical rule miss it: the capture is not zero-length, and the stream question -- which stream does the refusal travel on -- answers THE ONE YOU KEPT. ",

    "A grep for the receipt line over that file finds nothing and exits non-zero, which is indistinguishable from THE RECEIPT LINE IS ABSENT -- and absent would have meant the freshly promoted lane was consuming nothing and the promotion was cosmetic. ",

    "THE SHARPENING THIS INSTANCE ADDS is to the asymmetry claimed above: an empty capture never manufactures a false alarm is true of the CAPTURE and false of the CONSUMER, because a grep that searches for a symptom's ABSENCE converts the benign direction into a confident positive finding -- and a finding gets acted on where a green gets ignored, so the harm here is the greater one, not the lesser. ",

    "The rule that actually caught it is a THIRD beside the two above and is independent of both: size the artifact against what the subject plausibly weighs before reading a grep over it as a result. ",

    "Ninety-nine bytes is not a job log, whatever the exit code says. ",

    "FIFTH INSTANCE, 2026-09-02, gunbc PR 10086, AND IT IS A THIRD SHAPE RATHER THAN A REPEAT: A COMPLETED JOB WHOSE LOG READS ZERO BYTES WITH NO REFUSAL ON EITHER STREAM. ",

    "`gh run view --job 100322901366 --log` returned zero bytes and printed nothing on stderr -- not the documented in-progress refusal, no refusal at all -- while `gh api repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/actions/jobs/100322901366/logs --allow-escape-sequences` returned 442,248 bytes carrying the cause. ",

    "A grep over the empty capture finds nothing and exits non-zero, which reads as THE JOB LOG CONTAINS NO FAILURE for the very job that failed. ",

    "WHAT THIS INSTANCE BREAKS IS THE ROW ITSELF, and that is why it is filed rather than counted: the fallback advice accumulated above is CIRCULAR. ",

    "The fourth instance names `gh run view` as the escape from a refusing `gh api`; this instance names `gh api` as the escape from a silent `gh run view`. ",

    "The two routes are each other's documented remedy and both failed on 2026-09-02, in OPPOSITE directions -- ninety-nine bytes of refusal on the PAYLOAD channel from the api route, zero bytes and NO refusal from run view -- so a reader following this row lands on whichever route happens to be broken that day. ",

    "The two mechanical steps written above are route-dependent for one shared reason: each interrogates HOW THE INSTRUMENT REFUSED -- which stream the refusal travels on, what the exit status says -- and an instrument that emits no refusal at all answers neither question. ",

    "Consulting the typed status here yields SUCCESS over an empty capture, which is precisely the DID NOT READ case wearing the FOUND NOTHING answer. ",

    "ONLY THE SUBJECT-WEIGHT CHECK SURVIVES, and it survives because it interrogates the ARTIFACT rather than the instrument, so it is indifferent to which route broke. ",

    "COROLLARY, and it is the operative addition: when the weight is implausible, RE-READ BY THE OTHER ROUTE -- not because the other route is trustworthy, it demonstrably is not, but because 442,248 bytes against zero for one subject is a DISCRIMINATING COMPARISON, where either number read alone is not a measurement of anything.)  ",

    "COROLLARY CORRECTED, 2026-09-04, SAME REPOSITORY SAME DAY, BECAUSE THE SENTENCE ABOVE CAN BE READ AS NOMINATING A ROUTE AND THAT READING WOULD HAVE BEEN WRONG WITHIN HOURS. The fifth instance found `gh run view --job --log` returning ZERO while the API returned 442,248 bytes, which invites the rule re-read by the API. The inverse was then measured on three failing jobs of one run: `gh api .../actions/jobs/<id>/logs` returned ZERO BYTES for all three, while `gh run view --job <id> --log` returned 182,047, 871,334 and 6,171 bytes. NEITHER ROUTE IS THE RELIABLE ONE. ",

    "THE SYMMETRIC FORM, which is what this row now asserts: a zero-byte read is UNOBSERVED whichever route produced it, and the remedy is THE OTHER ROUTE, in whichever direction you started. The discriminating comparison is what carries the evidence -- one number against another for the same subject -- never the identity of the route that happened to answer. ",

    "AND A NON-EMPTY CAPTURE CAN ALSO BE PARTIAL, so the weight check is not only a test for suspiciously SMALL. One retry returned 1,048,662 bytes, which is 1 MiB plus 86 -- a cap plus a header or a partial final record, and FRONT-TRUNCATED, so the earliest lines were gone while the capture looked large and healthy. Note that a test for a suspiciously ROUND number would have MISSED it: 1,048,662 is not 1,048,576, and equality against a power of two fails. The tell is a value sitting JUST PAST a plausible limit rather than on it. ",

    "RECORDED BECAUSE OF HOW IT WAS FOUND: the author was capturing log evidence ABOUT THIS VERY CLASS when the API returned zero bytes, and came within one report of writing no matching lines found -- which would have been this class committed while documenting itself. That is the strongest available evidence that it recurs, and it is why the rule has to be mechanical rather than remembered. ",
    "SIXTH INSTANCE, 2026-09-04, import-cut lane, AND IT HARDENS A DIFFERENT HALF THAN THE FIFTH. The fifth hardens the READ -- an implausible capture weight, re-read by the other route. This one hardens the VERDICT ARM, and it is worth separating because a perfectly honest read can still be turned into a false green by how the arm is written. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN IS AN INSTRUMENT BUILT THAT AFTERNOON TO GUARD AGAINST THIS EXACT CLASS. A watcher polled CI for a green run whose floor had actually REACHED the parse phase, because a floor that aborts early silences later phases and the silence reads as a pass. Its verdict arm fetched the floor job log and grepped for FAILED PHASE and adjudication refusals. On an empty log -- a cancelled job, an unretained log, or precisely the zero-byte read the fifth instance documents -- grep matched nothing, and the arm would have reported a candidate green run carrying no failures. The author would have delivered a release recommendation derived from a log never read. ",

    "THE RULE, and it is stronger than sizing the capture at the reading site: A VERDICT WHOSE GREEN ARM IS THE ABSENCE OF BAD LINES CANNOT DISTINGUISH HEALTHY FROM UNREAD. Checking the capture helps only where the capture is checkable; the fifth instance already shows a route where the failure emits no refusal to interrogate, so the two mechanical steps are circular there. Requiring POSITIVE evidence is not route-dependent: the arm must find something that can only be present when the subject was genuinely observed. The repaired watcher requires the literal `phase parse (` announcement to be FOUND at least once before it will call anything a candidate, and prints UNOBSERVED with a reason at four separate points -- no such job, job conclusion not success, an EMPTY steps array, or an empty log. ",

    "WHY THE REPAIR GENERALISES BEYOND CAPTURES: the same shape is the heartbeat requirement on a deletion census. When a check PASSES by observing that things are gone, an instrument that observed NOTHING produces a perfect pass, so one known item must be held outside the deleted population and required present. Absence-as-success and absence-of-failure-as-success are the same defect, and positive evidence is the same repair.)",
    "SEVENTH INSTANCE, 2026-09-12, Mt. Collins unit 1 memory screen, AND IT DEFEATS EVERY RULE THIS ROW CARRIES, INCLUDING THE SUBJECT-WEIGHT CHECK THAT SURVIVED THE FIFTH. The subject is a STREAMING collector over a time window rather than a single read, which is the axis this row had not yet been tested on. `ipmitool sol activate` was run to observe host console output across a five-minute DRAM training window, eight times across eight hardware configurations, and every capture was reported as the console being silent. ",

    "WHAT THE CAPTURES ACTUALLY CONTAINED: the two lines `tcgetattr: Inappropriate ioctl for device` and `[SOL Session operational.  Use ~? for help]` and nothing else -- 86 bytes hashing to 3aea4368b8745ae7bdca3c7ec052a324032974f7b849bca460e7d0e14f5e0871, matched on all 64 hex characters by SEVEN of the eight files, the eighth being those same 86 bytes plus the wrapper own `done rc=0` trailer. Both lines are the INSTRUMENT own voice: the first is its local terminal warning, the second its own banner. ZERO host bytes were ever received in any capture. ",

    "WHY ALL THREE EXISTING RULES PASS. The stream question answers THE ONE YOU KEPT, as in the fourth instance. The typed status answers SUCCESS -- exit code 0, and unlike the fifth instance this is not a silent refusal wearing success, the client genuinely RAN and genuinely exited cleanly. And the subject-weight check, the one rule the fifth instance concluded survives because it interrogates the artifact rather than the instrument, ALSO PASSES: 86 bytes is exactly what this artifact should weigh when the console is quiet, so the weight is not implausible for the hypothesis being tested. ",

    "THE MECHANISM, and it is why a window changes the shape: stdin was not a terminal, which produced the tcgetattr warning; the client receive loop then reached stdin EOF and exited rc=0 after roughly three seconds; the surrounding wrapper slept out the remaining window and reported the unchanged file. So the instrument covered THREE SECONDS OF FOUR HUNDRED AND TWENTY and reported on all of them. A single read either happens or does not; a streaming collector can start, succeed, and be ABSENT for the interval whose emptiness is then consumed as a finding. ",

    "THE DISCRIMINATOR THAT WAS PRESENT AND UNREAD, and it is this instance operative addition: SEVEN CAPTURES OF SEVEN MATERIALLY DIFFERENT SUBJECTS WERE BYTE-IDENTICAL. Eight hardware configurations, three of which reached different boot outcomes -- one executed a kernel -- cannot produce one hash. For a streaming instrument, IDENTICAL CAPTURES ACROSS SUBJECTS THAT MUST DIFFER is the same kind of artifact-side evidence that implausible weight is for a single read, and it is available without interrogating the instrument at all. Nobody hashed them against each other for a week. ",

    "COVERAGE IS NOT READINESS, which is the modelling consequence. An activation acknowledgement earns nothing about the interval after it. A collector result must separate SESSION ACTIVATION ACKNOWLEDGED from COLLECTOR RUNNING from COVERAGE COMPLETE OR INTERRUPTED from HOST PAYLOAD RECEIVED OR NOT from TERMINATED WITH REASON, or `client exited early` and `subject produced nothing` remain one observation. The sixth instance rule is the one that would have caught this and it was not applied: the green arm here was the ABSENCE of host bytes, with no positive control establishing that this collector had ever successfully carried host output at all. ",

    "THE HARM WAS NOT THE EMPTY CAPTURE, IT WAS WHAT WAS BUILT ON IT. Three claims were reported to an operator and all three are retracted: that the platform firmware ignores the IPMI console-redirection request, that SOL silence is caused by host-side console routing, and that arming the BMC video and SOL recorders demonstrably fails to open the pre-OS window. None had any evidence, because the console was never observed. A fourth consequence reached a pull request: a sibling lane modelled present-but-silent SOL as a FACT ABOUT THE HOST in extdeps.bmc.megarac, which had to be retracted before it landed. This is the class propagating from a bad reading into the corpus as an upstream property, which is also a DESIGN section 3 layer inversion -- an observation copied upward into extdeps. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent wrongness for a week, then mitigatable once the captures were hashed against each other. The finding came from a REVIEWING SESSION reconstructing the two lines from their published byte count and digest prefix, not from the author, and not from any check. ",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable for collectors this repository owns -- a result type in which coverage and payload are separate fields cannot represent `exited at three seconds` as `observed for four hundred and twenty`. It stays mitigatable for third-party clients whose stdin and lifetime discipline is outside the modeled guarantee. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a streaming-observation carrier whose value cannot be consumed as a negative observation unless it holds BOTH a completed-coverage interval AND a positive control establishing that this collector instance has carried subject payload at least once, sufficient that a client which exited before its window closed has no constructor for `subject produced nothing`. A meta file recording the child pid and exit status does not discharge this: the seventh instance status was SUCCESS and the defect survived it. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, artifact-side and therefore route-independent like the weight check: before believing that a streaming instrument observed nothing, hash its captures against each other. Identical bytes across subjects that MUST differ is a strong tell.",

    "CORRECTED ON THE SAME DAY IT WAS WRITTEN, BY THE OPERATOR, AND THE CORRECTION IS THE POINT: identical hashes are a SUSPICION TRIGGER, NOT PROOF OF SELF-OBSERVATION. Two legitimate readings of one genuinely-quiet channel are also identical, and so are two runs of a subject that did not in fact differ in what it emitted -- so the hash comparison can only raise the question, never answer it. Treating it as proof would be this row's own defect one level up: a cheap artifact-side signal promoted to a verdict because it is cheap.",

    "WHAT ACTUALLY DECIDES IT is the conjunction, and no member of it suffices alone: the captures compared against each other; the EXPECTED STIMULUS (was the subject known to be emitting during the window -- the seventh instance had three configurations reaching different boot outcomes, one executing a kernel, which is what made identical bytes impossible rather than merely suspicious); COVERAGE (what fraction of the window the collector was demonstrably alive and attached for); and PROCESS OR SESSION EVIDENCE (child pid, start and end, exit status, and whether the exit preceded the window's close). Require additionally that the collector has carried a positive payload on this EXACT path at least once, because a path that has never delivered anything cannot distinguish a quiet subject from a broken client.",

    "THE OPERATOR'S SHARPENING GENERALISES the same way the fifth instance's did: interrogating the INSTRUMENT is route-dependent and interrogating the ARTIFACT is not, but an artifact-side signal still only bounds the hypothesis space. Absence of an expected difference is evidence about the observation; it is not yet a fact about the subject.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
